<title>HONG KONG: China Motor Bus 1995/96 net down 79 pct.</title>
<headline>China Motor Bus 1995/96 net down 79 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   135.0  vs 642.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    76.0   vs 76.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs 189.44 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    62.26  vs 297.07</p>
<p>    Turnover		     773.56 vs 785.43</p>
<p>    Company name		 China Motor Bus Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  November 29-December 12</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   December 16</p>
<p>NOTE - China Motor Bus operates franchised public buses in Hong Kong. It also declares a special dividend of HK$2 vs nil.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 378 H.K. cents (including three special dividends, interim dividend and second interim dividend) vs 192 cents (including special dividend, interim dividend and second interim dividend).</p>
<p>The group pays two interim dividends and one final dividend a year.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
